  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "getGREVersion",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/GreLayer.cpp",
    "description": "GreLayer::getGREVersion() accepts any 4-byte gre_basic_header and returns GREv1 solely from its version bits, although GREv1 requires the 8-byte gre1_header. IPv4Layer/IPv6Layer consequently construct a GREv1Layer over truncated packet data. Later GREv1Layer::computeCalculateFields() unconditionally writes the 2-byte gre1_header::payloadLength at m_Data+4 (GreLayer.cpp:539), overflowing when fewer than 6 bytes\u2014and in this PoV, only 4 bytes\u2014remain. Validation should reject GREv1 data shorter than sizeof(gre1_header) before constructing the layer.",
    "conditions": "A parsed IPv4 or IPv6 packet must designate GRE as its next protocol and leave a truncated GRE payload of at least sizeof(gre_basic_header) (4 bytes) but less than sizeof(gre1_header) (8 bytes), with the low three version bits in GRE byte 1 equal to 1. The PoV supplies exactly 4 GRE bytes at the end of the captured packet, so getGREVersion() returns GREv1 and a GREv1Layer points at the final 4 bytes of the pcap-allocated packet buffer. When the harness calls Packet::computeCalculateFields(), the payloadLength write at offset 4 crosses the heap allocation boundary."
  },
